    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>keeps the internal buffers of the sweep-line triangulation alive between runs, so a caller triangulating many contour sets one by one avoids re-allocating them on every call; the entries returning a <ref refid="structMR_1_1Mesh" kindref="compound">Mesh</ref> move the topology and the points out into it, so those two grow again on the next run, while <ref refid="group__GeneralGroup_1ga2f9e9b49c88ebf29c5a8a41b0659b9a4" kindref="member">triangulateDisjointContoursTopology</ref> keeps everything; one cache must not be used by several threads at once </para>
    </detaileddescription>
